    "datePublished": "2026-04-10",
    "dateModified": "2026-04-24",
    "readingMinutes": 6,
    "category": "Comparison Guide",
    "html": "<a href=\"/blog\" class=\"blog-back\"><i class=\"ph-bold ph-arrow-left\"></i> Back to Blog</a>\r\n        <div class=\"badge\">Comparison Guide</div>\r\n        <h1>Maid vs Cook vs Nanny: Which Home Help Do You Actually Need?</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"blog-meta\">\r\n          <span><i class=\"ph-bold ph-calendar\"></i> April 10, 2026</span>\r\n          <span><i class=\"ph-bold ph-clock\"></i> 6 min read</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p>One of the most common questions we get from families is: <em>\"I need help at home, but I'm not sure what kind.\"</em> Should you hire a part-time maid? A full-time cook? A nanny? Or maybe a live-in helper who does everything?</p>\r\n        <p>Let's break down each type so you can make the right choice.</p>\r\n\r\n        <h2>Quick Comparison Table</h2>\r\n        <div style=\"overflow-x:auto\">\r\n        <table class=\"blog-table\">\r\n          <thead>\r\n            <tr>\r\n              <th>Type</th>\r\n              <th>Best For</th>\r\n              <th>Hours</th>\r\n              <th>Salary (Metro)</th>\r\n            </tr>\r\n          </thead>\r\n          <tbody>\r\n            <tr><td><strong>Part-Time Maid</strong></td><td>Working couples, small apartments</td><td>4-6 hrs/day</td><td>₹8K – ₹12K/mo</td></tr>\r\n            <tr><td><strong>Full-Time Maid</strong></td><td>Large families, bigger homes</td><td>8-12 hrs/day</td><td>₹12K – ₹18K/mo</td></tr>\r\n            <tr><td><strong>Specialized Cook</strong></td><td>Health-conscious families</td><td>3-5 hrs/day</td><td>₹10K – ₹15K/mo</td></tr>\r\n            <tr><td><strong>Nanny / Babysitter</strong></td><td>Working parents with young kids</td><td>8-12 hrs/day</td><td>₹14K – ₹20K/mo</td></tr>\r\n            <tr><td><strong>Elderly Caregiver</strong></td><td>Families with aging parents</td><td>12-24 hrs/day</td><td>₹15K – ₹22K/mo</td></tr>\r\n            <tr><td><strong>Live-In Helper</strong></td><td>Joint families, NRI homes</td><td>24/7</td><td>₹18K – ₹25K/mo</td></tr>\r\n          </tbody>\r\n        </table>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <h2>1. Part-Time Maid</h2>\r\n        <p><strong>What they do:</strong> Cleaning, mopping, dishes, laundry, and light kitchen work.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Ideal for:</strong> Working professionals and couples who need daily upkeep but don't require full-day help. Most common in urban apartments.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Typical schedule:</strong> Morning (7-11 AM) or split shift (7-9 AM + 5-7 PM).</p>\r\n\r\n        <h2>2. Specialized Cook</h2>\r\n        <p><strong>What they do:</strong> Meal planning, preparation, and kitchen management tailored to your dietary preferences.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Ideal for:</strong> Families who value nutrition, have dietary restrictions, or simply don't have time to cook. Especially popular with health-conscious professionals and families with specific cuisine needs (Jain, diabetic-friendly, etc.).</p>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"blog-tip\">\r\n          <p><strong>💡 Tip:</strong> When hiring a cook, always conduct a trial cooking session. Ask them to prepare 2-3 dishes from your regular menu to assess taste, hygiene, and speed.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <h2>3. Nanny / Babysitter</h2>\r\n        <p><strong>What they do:</strong> Childcare, feeding, bathing, school pickup/drop, play supervision, and developmental activities.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Ideal for:</strong> Dual-income families or single parents with children under 10. A good nanny becomes an extension of the family.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Critical requirement:</strong> Patience, first-aid knowledge, and genuine affection for children. Always prioritize personality over price.</p>\r\n\r\n        <h2>4. Elderly Caregiver</h2>\r\n        <p><strong>What they do:</strong> Mobility assistance, medication reminders, meal prep, companionship, and emergency response.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Ideal for:</strong> NRI families with parents in India, or working professionals who can't be home during the day. Increasingly in demand across India.</p>\r\n\r\n        <h2>5. Live-In Helper</h2>\r\n        <p><strong>What they do:</strong> Complete household management — cleaning, cooking, laundry, childcare, and general upkeep.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Ideal for:</strong> Large families, joint families, or homes with multiple needs. The all-in-one solution.</p>\r\n        <p><strong>Note:</strong> Live-in helpers require accommodation (a separate room or at least a private sleeping area), meals, and one weekly day off.</p>\r\n\r\n        <h2>How to Decide?</h2>\r\n        <p>Ask yourself these 3 questions:</p>\r\n        <ul>\r\n          <li><strong>What's my biggest pain point?</strong> Cleaning → Maid. Cooking → Cook. Kids → Nanny.</li>\r\n          <li><strong>How many hours of help do I need?</strong> Under 6 hours → Part-time. Over 8 → Full-time or live-in.</li>\r\n          <li><strong>What's my budget?</strong> Start with one role and expand as needed.</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"blog-cta-box\">\r\n          <h3>Not Sure? Let Us Help You Decide</h3>\r\n          <p>Tell us your needs and we'll recommend the perfect Buddy for your household.</p>\r\n          <a href=\"/\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Book a Free Consultation</a>\r\n        </div>"
